Subject: Reuse realloc capacity when PHP grows strings under Fil-C
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

Fil-C's realloc() always allocates a new object, copies and frees the
old one, and zend_string_extend() asks for the exact new length, so
`$s .= ...` copied the whole string on every append: building an n-byte
string took O(n^2), and Zend/bench.php's strcat took 11 s instead of
0.02 s. On the system allocator (php-8.4-alloc-filc.patch), grow past
1 KiB by half again and reuse that capacity, which zgetupper() reports,
as Zend's allocator and glibc's in-place realloc do. The capability then
also spans the slack, which realloc() zeroed, or after a shrink to no
less than half the capacity, the old contents.

--- a/Zend/zend_alloc.c
+++ b/Zend/zend_alloc.c
@@ -64,6 +64,9 @@
 #include "zend_string.h"
 #include "zend_exceptions.h"
 #include <signal.h>
+#ifdef __FILC__
+# include <stdfil.h>
+#endif
 
 #ifdef HAVE_UNISTD_H
 # include <unistd.h>
@@ -3996,6 +3999,24 @@ ZEND_API void * __zend_calloc(size_t nmemb, size_t len ZEND_FILE_LINE_DC ZEND_FI
 
 ZEND_API void * __zend_realloc(void *p, size_t len ZEND_FILE_LINE_DC ZEND_FILE_LINE_ORIG_DC)
 {
+#ifdef __FILC__
+	/* Fil-C's realloc() always moves the object, so growing a string one
+	 * append at a time (zend_string_extend() asks for the exact length)
+	 * copied the whole string each time: building an n-byte string took
+	 * O(n^2). Grow by half again past 1 KiB and reuse the slack, as Zend's
+	 * allocator and glibc's in-place realloc do. The capability then spans
+	 * the slack, which is zeroed, or after a shrink to no less than half the
+	 * capacity, the old contents. */
+	if (p && len) {
+		size_t cap = (char *) zgetupper(p) - (char *) p;
+		if (len <= cap && len >= cap / 2) {
+			return p;
+		}
+		if (len > cap && len > 1024 && len < cap + cap / 2) {
+			len = cap + cap / 2;
+		}
+	}
+#endif
 	p = realloc(p, len);
 	if (EXPECTED(p || !len)) {
 		return p;
